[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h1.png[/img][/center]

[font=Roboto]Manage what you and your NPCs wear, save their current equipment as outfits, and switch outfits automatically to suit the situation.
Aim at an NPC and press [b][color=#EAD08F]Shift + V[/color][/b]. Aim anywhere else to open Livery on yourself.[/font]

[center][youtube]cs3NHxkLKH8[/youtube][/center]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h2_features.png[/img][/center]
[font=Roboto][b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Dress NPCs ◆[/color][/size][/b]

✧ Change an NPC's equipment through a dedicated interface, using items from their inventory or yours.
✧ Live Preview keeps the game running while you dress. Move, rotate and zoom the camera to check every angle.
✧ What you put on stays on: no swapping, no drifting back.

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Save Outfits ◆[/color][/size][/b]

✧ Save what they're wearing as an outfit, straight from their equipment.
✧ It hangs in your Wardrobe, ready to wear whenever you like.

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Situational Outfits ◆[/color][/size][/b]

✧ Assign outfits for Town, Castle, Home, Sleep or Cold (rain, snow or the snowy north).
✧ Livery switches them automatically, with assignments saved per character.
✧ Assign several outfits to a situation and Livery picks one at random whenever it becomes active.

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Item Chests ◆[/color][/size][/b]

✧ Organise equipment into custom chests you can access while dressing characters.
✧ Should come in handy for armor mods with lots of variants.
[color=#9f9f9f]Off by default; turn it on in the settings.[/color][/font]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h2_philosophy.png[/img][/center]
[font=Roboto][b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Simple and Streamlined ◆[/color][/size][/b]

✧ Intuitive interface: aim, press the hotkey, select the items, Apply.
✧ Lightweight by design: an SKSE plugin only. No ESP or ESM in your load order, no Papyrus scripts in the background.

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Immersion-Conscious ◆[/color][/size][/b]

[color=#b7da7b][size=3][i]An interface that belongs in Skyrim[/i][/size][/color]
✧ Three skins cut to fit Skyrim: Vanilla, Nordic and Modern. Every colour is yours to change.
✧ A window that looks and handles like Skyrim's own menus, with familiar SkyUI item icons.
✧ Compact, so the NPC stays in view: dressing them feels like part of the conversation, not a trip to a menu.
✧ Open Livery on an NPC and they'll turn to face you and greet you. (Configurable)

[color=#b7da7b][size=3][i]Respect for the game's rules[/i][/size][/color]
✧ By default, Livery dresses only you, your followers and your spouse. (Configurable)
✧ Friends let you save their outfit, much as the game lets you help yourself to their things. (Configurable)
✧ An outfit is built from equipment that actually exists in someone's inventory, or from the NPC's current outfit, not from a plugin's item list.
✧ By default, you can only wear items you actually carry. (Configurable)

[color=#b7da7b][size=3][i]No free items, no lost equipment[/i][/size][/color]
✧ Saving or switching an outfit never consumes an item.
✧ Items Livery creates for an NPC's outfit cannot be taken from them through trading.

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Your Game, Your Rules ◆[/color][/size][/b]

Livery's defaults lean towards immersion, but they're not there to tell you how to play.
Everything marked (Configurable) is a setting: tighten the rules or loosen them.[/font]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h2_quickstart.png[/img][/center]
[font=Roboto][b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Opening Livery ◆[/color][/size][/b]

Press the hotkey ([b][color=#EAD08F]Shift + V[/color][/b] by default).
Aim at an NPC to open Livery on them; aim anywhere else to open it on yourself.

By default, you can dress your followers and spouse and save what your friends wear. 
Other NPCs are off limits. (Configurable)

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Dress a follower or your spouse ◆[/color][/size][/b][/font]

[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_dress.png][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_dress_thumb.png[/img][/url]

[list=1]
[*][font=Roboto]Open Livery on the NPC.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Select the items you want them to wear.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][b][color=#EAD08F]Apply[/color][/b], then [b][color=#EAD08F]Exit[/color][/b].[/font][/*]
[/list]
[font=Roboto]- [b][color=#EAD08F]Add from Wardrobe...[/color][/b] puts a saved outfit's items on the list.

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Save an outfit ◆[/color][/size][/b][/font]

[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_create.png][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_create_thumb.png[/img][/url]

[list=1]
[*][font=Roboto]Open Livery on yourself or the NPC, wearing what you want to save. A friend in something you like works too.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Press [b][color=#EAD08F]Save to Wardrobe...[/color][/b][/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Name it, pick an icon, [b][color=#EAD08F]Create[/color][/b].[/font][/*]
[/list]
[font=Roboto]- To change an existing outfit, use the [b][color=#EAD08F]Update[/color][/b] tab.

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Wear an outfit from the Wardrobe ◆[/color][/size][/b][/font]

[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_wardrobe.png][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_wardrobe_thumb.png[/img][/url]

[list=1]
[*][font=Roboto]Pick the [b][color=#EAD08F]Wardrobe[/color][/b] tab on the left.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Select an outfit.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][b][color=#EAD08F]Apply[/color][/b], then [b][color=#EAD08F]Exit[/color][/b].[/font][/*]
[/list]
[font=Roboto]- Rename an outfit, change its icon or remove it on the same page.
- You can also choose which items to wear without changing the saved outfit.

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Set situational outfits ◆[/color][/size][/b][/font]

[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_situation.png][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_situation_thumb.png[/img][/url]

[list=1]
[*][font=Roboto]Pick the [b][color=#EAD08F]Situations[/color][/b] tab on the left.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Drag outfits from the list on the right onto the situations on the left. They are saved as you go.[/font][/*]
[/list]
[font=Roboto]- Drag an outfit back to the list to remove it from a situation.
- Assign several outfits to a situation for a random pick each time it becomes active. Assignments are saved per character.

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Use item chests ◆[/color][/size][/b]

[youtube]GbQ1esHAYW0[/youtube]

Turn on [b][color=#EAD08F]Enable chests[/color][/b] in the settings first.[/font]

[list=1]
[*][font=Roboto]Pick the [b][color=#EAD08F]Chests[/color][/b] tab, press [b][color=#EAD08F]Create New Chest...[/color][/b] and name it.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Click items from your inventory or the NPC's to put them in. [b][color=#EAD08F]Add from Wardrobe...[/color][/b] puts in a whole outfit.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]When dressing, press [b][color=#EAD08F]Add from Chest...[/color][/b], select the chest, [b][color=#EAD08F]Load[/color][/b]. Select the items you want, then [b][color=#EAD08F]Apply[/color][/b].[/font][/*]
[/list]
[font=Roboto]- From the chest editor, [b][color=#EAD08F]Dress with this Chest...[/color][/b] takes you straight to the Dress page with its items already on the list.[/font]

[font=Roboto][b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Configure Livery ◆[/color][/size][/b]

[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_skin.png][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/desc_skin_thumb.png[/img][/url]

Settings are available on the Livery page of SKSE Menu Framework, or in [font=Courier New][color=#a7c17b]Data\SKSE\Plugins\Livery.ini[/color][/font] (read when the game starts).

The window's Appearance tab lets you change the skin, palette and menu sounds, even without SKSE Menu Framework.

To change the window's colours, edit the #RRGGBB values in your palette's .ini under [font=Courier New]Data\SKSE\Plugins\Livery\palettes\[/font], or copy one under a new name and edit the copy.
[b][color=#EAD08F]Restore original palette[/color][/b] on the Appearance tab undoes edits to a shipped palette.[/font]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h2_requirements.png[/img][/center]
[list]
[*][font=Roboto]Skyrim SE or AE. Built for SE 1.5.97 and AE 1.6.x and 1.7.x.
Tested on 1.6.1170; reports from other versions welcome, with your Livery.log.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url][/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url] for SE and AE, matching your game version (1.7.x needs a recent release)[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/120352]SKSE Menu Framework[/url], for changing the settings in game[/font][/*]
[/list]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h2_installation.png[/img][/center]
[list=1]
[*][font=Roboto]Install the requirements above.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Install Livery via your mod manager.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Launch Skyrim via SKSE.[/font][/*]
[/list]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h2_compatibility.png[/img][/center]
[font=Roboto]Other outfit managers may interfere with Livery's dressing, especially automatic outfit switching. 
It's best to let one mod handle each character's outfits.[/font]

[font=Roboto][b]Nether's Follower Framework[/b]: fine, as long as you don't use its outfit features on the followers Livery dresses.

Skyrim VR is not supported (I don't own it to test).[/font]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h2_uninstall.png[/img][/center]
[font=Roboto]Before uninstalling, I recommend pressing [b][color=#EAD08F]Release everyone[/color][/b] in SKSE Menu Framework, or setting [font=Courier New]ReleaseEveryone=1[/font] under [font=Courier New][Uninstall][/font] in Livery.ini and loading your save. This unlocks NPCs Livery dressed and takes back the items it gave them.
If you skip this step, those NPCs keep their outfits locked on, and Livery-created items become lootable.[/font]
Then remove Livery; it adds no plugin file, so your save loads without it.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h2_faq.png[/img][/center]
[font=Roboto][b][color=#a7c17b]An NPC changed back after a bath or a scene.[/color][/b]
By design. Livery puts the outfit back on when the NPC's 3D loads or their situation changes, not every frame, so other mods can undress them for a while.

[b][color=#a7c17b]I added an item to an Outfit or Chest, but it's still in my inventory.[/color][/b]
Think of Outfits and Chests as lists of items, not storage containers. Adding an item to a list doesn't make the actual item disappear. 
When dressing a character, Livery uses the items they already have or provides what's missing.

[b][color=#a7c17b]I can't wear an outfit myself.[/color][/b]
By default, Livery won't provide missing items to the player. You might just sell them!
Turn off [b][color=#EAD08F]Dress yourself from inventory only[/color][/b] to allow it.
Also, items Livery provides to NPCs can't be taken through trading.

[b][color=#a7c17b]Does Livery keep my enchantments and tempering?[/color][/b]
Outfits and Chests remember which items you added, not the exact copies. They don't store your enchantments or tempering.
When dressing, Livery picks the best matching copy the character carries: a player-enchanted one first, then the most tempered, then a plain one.
Enchanted items from a plugin, like a Ring of Alchemy, are items in their own right and keep their effect.

[b][color=#a7c17b]An NPC won't equip gear I give them—or equips gear I don't want them to.[/color][/b]
NPCs won't replace gear assigned by Livery. To change it, edit their outfit in Livery instead.
Empty slots work differently: by default, NPCs can equip extra gear there, except headgear, so a shield goes on and a helmet comes off again.
You can change this under [b][color=#EAD08F]Gear in unused slots[/color][/b] in Settings.

[b][color=#a7c17b]My Sleep outfit never goes on.[/color][/b]
The game's own beds just pass the time. It goes on with a mod that actually puts you into bed.

[b][color=#a7c17b]My sleep mod has its own sleepwear. Which should I use?[/color][/b]
Either, but one per character. 
Turn the other mod's sleepwear off for the characters Livery dresses, or leave their Sleep situation empty.

[b][color=#a7c17b]Where is my outfit data stored?[/color][/b]
[font=Courier New]Data\SKSE\Plugins\Livery\outfits.json[/font], shared by all saves. 
Items are stored by plugin name and FormID, so outfits survive a load order change. Back it up with your saves.

[b][color=#a7c17b]The hotkey only shows "Livery: the window is not available."[/color][/b]
Livery couldn't set up its window in this game. 
The usual cause is a game version it doesn't handle yet; Livery.log says what it found. Please send it with your game version.

[b][color=#a7c17b]I can take the items Livery made for an NPC by trading with them.[/color][/b]
Livery hides them in the trade, pickpocket and container menus. 
If they show anyway, your game version may be one Livery doesn't handle yet; Livery.log says what it found. 
Please send it with your game version.

[b][color=#a7c17b]Something went wrong. Where do I look?[/color][/b]
[font=Courier New]Documents\My Games\Skyrim Special Edition\SKSE\Livery.log[/font].[/font]


[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yirny/Livery/main/docs/assets/nexus/h2_roadmap.png[/img][/center]
[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ In progress ◆[/color][/size][/b]

[list]
[*][font=Roboto][b]Custom situations[/b]: add your own, and edit their conditions.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][b]Non-ASCII names[/b], so you can name an outfit in your own language.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][b]Livery API[/b], so other mods can use its dressing and outfits.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ Ideas, not planned yet (tell me which you'd use) ◆[/color][/size][/b]

[list]
[*][font=Roboto][b]Layered outfits[/b] that go over your current one, e.g. a hood and cloak for cold weather. 
Should be handy, but a second kind of outfit to keep track of.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][b]Custom tags[/b] on outfits, like "Light Armor", "Casual" or a mod author's name. 
Easier to find things, but busier lists. 
For now, icons and colours are the way to organise.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][b]A wardrobe per save[/b]. 
Outfits would belong to the playthrough: nothing from items this character never found. 
But losing your outfit edits because you died before saving the game would feel silly too. 
For now, managing [font=Courier New]outfits.json[/font] by hand gets you part of the way.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][b]Opening Livery from dialogue[/b]. 
More immersive, but it needs an ESP.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][b]A middle ground for wearing items you don't own[/b]: today it's a free armoury or nothing. 
Spawned items could vanish when taken off, or count as stolen, as if you'd lifted them somewhere.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto][b]Poses[/b] for the NPC while you dress them. 
Nice for checking the fit, but perhaps a little beyond what Livery is for.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[b][size=4][color=#a7c17b]◆ What Livery won't do ◆[/color][/size][/b]

[list]
[*][font=Roboto]Pull armor straight out of plugins. 
Some other outfit managers do that well; or run an AddItemMenu-type mod beside Livery.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Roboto]Enforce an outfit every frame. 
Livery updates at set moments, so other mods' temporary changes are allowed and the game stays light.[/font][/*]
[/list]


